Completing the square on $x$, we add $(2/2)^2=1$ to both sides, and on $y$, we add $(4/2)^2=4$ to both sides, to get
\begin{align*}
9(x^2-2x+1)+9(y^2+4y+4)&=-44+9+36\\
9(x-1)^2+9(y+2)^2&=1.
\end{align*}
Dividing both sides by $9$, we have $(x-1)^2+(y+2)^2=\frac{1}{9}$.
This is the equation of a circle with center $(1,-2)$ and radius $\sqrt{\frac{1}{9}}=\boxed{\frac{1}{3}}$.
